{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "source": {
    "chests": "Ids 910100-910104 are reconstructed (no catalogue holds a Type 28 chest). Each row is the chest opened in the real client on 2026-10-09 (lab report mystery-chest-intake-20261009T192906Z: Type 28, category 408, rarity 3, no trade, no sale, single use), with the series' client text (locale) and icon (Resources/Images/ImageSets.txt mysterychest, mysterychest_scifi, mysterychest_sunstone, mysterychest_seasonal, mysterychest_genie).",
    "prizes": "Prize definitions the shipped inventory and item table lack, from the FreeRealms-Legacy@9e08202 ClientItemDefinitions (AGPL-3.0-or-later), each identical in Sanctuary-main@10f129e; the base tint variant of each set piece.",
    "series": {
      "910100": "Original (Series 1)",
      "910101": "Sci-Fi (Series 2)",
      "910102": "Clockwork (Series 3, mysterychest_sunstone)",
      "910103": "Snow Days (seasonal; no description of its own, the series' shared line)",
      "910104": "Chest of Wonders (mysterychest_genie)"
    },
    "recipe_outputs": "Ids 910200-910226 are reconstructed (2026-11-07): crafting outputs the server never sent (recipes_unresolved.json names them). Name and description are the client's own text ids for that name; icon, model, slot, type, category, rank and rarity follow the closest existing item of the same kind (lab/tools/item_reconstruct.py) (R).",
    "rides": "34 ride items (Type 19) that stores.json and mounts.json name but the original (PS3-era) item table lacks, from the FreeRealms-Legacy@9e08202 ClientItemDefinitions (AGPL-3.0-or-later), each identical in Sanctuary-main@10f129e except nine rows (78332, 78394-78396, 79413, 79434, 79435, 79442, 79446) where the two differ in stack size or the tintable flag and Sanctuary-main's values, the original table's own ride convention (stack 1), are used; model names match the client's Models.txt and names the client locale (lab/tools/donor_item_rows.py). Unknown36 carries the ride's mount id (the donor's Param1), as the original table's own ride rows do.",
    "collection_rewards": "(R) 2026-11-09: two collection reward items no item table defines, so the captured reward rows could not be granted. 38816 Skullz Tent and 38817 Sunstone Street Lamp are the ids the 2014 login capture carries on the Sunstone Valley Elite and Rare Exploration reward rows; the wiki names both rewards; name ids are the client's own text (33940, 33942), model and icon are the client's own files (hsg_tents_skullz_01.adr with image set 74, hsg_sunstone_street_lamp_01.adr with image set 8000), and the other columns follow the nearest housing rows (16875 Medium Tent, 18152 Tall Street Lamp). The third skipped reward, 79446 Skeletal T-Rex (Sunstone Valley Explorer), is defined by the mounts piece's row.",
    "bank": "P-banking (2026-11-11). Ids 35853-35862 are the client's ten Coin Shop bank upgrades, from the FreeRealms-Legacy@9e08202 ClientItemDefinitions (AGPL-3.0-or-later): name, description, icon (ImageSets 8131 bank_upgrade_coin), type 30, category 62, stack 1, member discount, the NoTrade/NoSale/ForceDisablePreview flags, and Unknown36 = the donor's Param1, the slots the upgrade adds. Cost (R) is the wiki Banking page's coin price (1,000 to 50,000): the donor's Cost (5 to 50) is not a coin price. Id 910900 is the Storage Vault (R): the client's own model hsg_storage_vault_01.adr (Models.txt 4443, in the community asset manifest), name 2601 'Bank', description 14142 (the 'Visit a Robgoblin Banker today!' tip), icon 93 category_bank, and the Storage Rack's (16850) housing columns (type 1, category 53, rank 1, stack 1); no trade or sale. Id 35852 is the 50-Slot Bank Upgrade the Marketplace sold for 100 Station Cash with no purchase limit (wiki); the same donor columns (icon 8132 bank_upgrade_sc, stack unlimited, Class 168, rarity 3). Cost (R) is 25,000 coins: no Marketplace shelf lists bank upgrades here, so it is a repeatable Coin Shop upgrade at the ten upgrades' own rate of 500 coins a slot."
  },
